    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256">

                <pb facs="0407" n="315" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg315"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/1952</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-25T17:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 25, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6.12 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2205. Your 1569, September 24, 3 p.m. No knowledge I have or can obtain at
                    present leads me to believe that the British Government is preparing to consider
                    favorably such a proposition but I shall keep the matter in mind and report
                    anything that appears to indicate a tendency in this direction.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
